#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101763} :activity/id #uuid "0dbeb966-d2d7-56fc-87f7-9f532b108178" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050912 :topic/id #uuid "70abc32f-7c95-5eaa-bc37-2779f513c439" :topic/math-academy-id 1174} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101763 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101920 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we have an alternating series\n\n$$\nS = \\sum_{n =1}^\\infty b_n\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nb_n = (-1)^n a_n\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nb_n = (-1)^{n+1} a_n\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\na_n \\geq 0\n$$\n\nLet's assume that the above series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\nThe $N$th partial sum of this series is\n\n$$\ns_n = \\sum_{n =1}^N b_n\n$$\n\nHow good an estimate of $S$ is the $n$th partial sum of $S$?\n\nThe **alternating series error bound** states that, for a convergent alternating series,\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}S- s_n & < & b_{n+1}\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the magnitude of the error of the $n$th partial sum is less than the magnitude of the $(n+1)$th term." :tutorial/id #uuid "d1ab9f29-4499-5933-a4db-cf6fd5292dd6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1260 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "cc3fd837-dffb-53ad-8a81-f754a99bdf38" :step/math-academy-id 2473 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101764}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101764 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100924 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100772 :question/id #uuid "dfa7cfd6-08dd-507f-aa3a-61beacbc36ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-721"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1ad1fe5-c690-54ab-a172-fdc69668d60d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050417}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101191} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101467} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536809}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Alternating Series Error Bound for a Given Partial Sum"} :step/id #uuid "a6217776-80ac-51aa-9ea0-f5fce39fdb15" :step/math-academy-id 2474 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101765}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101765 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100925 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100774 :question/id #uuid "193d6ccc-ffa5-5f36-8ed1-084dea29448f" :question/math-academy-id "e-723"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "be83d82e-531e-52bf-bacb-b621694ce40c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048159}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101186} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101464}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Values of N Such That the Error in the Nth Partial Sum Is Smaller Than a Given Number"} :step/id #uuid "05d18ce2-c320-5098-8bb6-ce9ee0b599e9" :step/math-academy-id 2480}] :activity/title "The Alternating Series Error Bound" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186101041}]}
